Done. Summary:

**Reproduced** (pre-fix, on `bd59fde`): a nested declaration lost its enclosing bindings (`nothing` instead of `5`), two same-named nested declarations shared one body (`nothing`/`nothing` instead of `2`/`101`), and an aliased call found no body (`nothing` instead of `5`).

**Decision: real closures.** `Value::Function(String, Vec<String>)` → `Value::Function(FunctionValue)`, where `FunctionValue` carries the name, params, `Arc<Vec<Stmt>>` body and `Arc<Captured>` environment. The body-by-name `HashMap` is deleted. Policy: capture **by value at declaration time**, globals read live, params above captures, captures above the caller's frames, `set_var` now resolves a name exactly as `get_var` does (required for by-value capture to be coherent — without it a body assigning a captured name wrote a global).

**Tests**: `tests/closure_capture_test.rs` (26 `#[test]`, 15 `edge_*`, 4 assert a failure) + `tests/test_closures.rb` (16 blocks, 25 `expect`s). Verified non-vacuous: stashing the src changes makes 11 of the 16 Redblue blocks fail, and the first Rust test failed red for the right reason before any production edit.

**Gates**: `cargo fmt --check` pass · `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings` pass (0 warnings) · `cargo test --all-targets` **197 passed, 0 failed** · `./rbops/verify.sh` **not run — `rbops/` does not exist in this checkout**; its examples+suite portion run directly (6 examples + `SuiteKit.rb` exit 0; `rb test` 219/219; `rb lint` clean on all 12 `tests/*.rb`).

`phases/phase-011/REPORT.md` and `phases/phase-011/FINDINGS.md` written. FINDINGS record four out-of-scope defects found on the way, the largest being that `give back` does not leave a function (so every recursive program, including these tests, must compute a result into a variable and return it after the block).

DONE
